@TITLE@ QilinRecomp for Windows (64-bit)
====================================

APB - All Points Bulletin (@STUDIO@), recompiled to run
natively: the arcade board's two processors' programs translated into
C++ and compiled for your PC, checked against MAME's processor
cores, drawn with Vulkan.

No game data is included. You need your own copy of the ROMs:
@RELEASE@ (136051-1101.5t to 136051-7129.6n),
unzipped into a folder of their own.
MAME's apb.zip is that set zipped: unzip it first.


Playing
-------
1. Unzip the download anywhere. Building the game needs about 1 GB free.
2. Open the folder and double-click "Play @TITLE@.exe".
3. Click "Choose your ROM set" and pick the folder holding the ROM files,
   or drag the folder onto the window. It tells you straight away if files
   are missing or damaged, or if it is another revision of APB.
4. Wait for the first build: a few minutes. Your ROMs never leave your PC.
5. Click Play. The window hides while the game runs. "Add a desktop
   shortcut" puts Play @TITLE@ on your desktop.

After that, Play @TITLE@.exe remembers your ROM folder (even in a new
download folder), and Play starts the game straight away. After an update
it builds the game again first, recompiling only what changed.

The game's output is in work\run.log and work\run-errors.log, and the
build's in work\build.log. Send them when reporting a problem.

If Windows says "Windows protected your PC": More info, then Run anyway.
(The download isn't signed.) Or before unpacking, right-click the zip,
Properties, tick Unblock, OK.

Needs: Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and a graphics driver with Vulkan 1.3
(any recent NVIDIA, AMD or Intel driver).


Controls
--------
Keyboard: arrows steer and accelerate; Left Ctrl, Left Alt, Space are the
siren/start, fire and alternate siren; 5 inserts a coin. Gamepad: left stick
or d-pad steers, right trigger or d-pad up accelerates, A or Start
starts/sirens, B fires, X is alternate siren, Back (View) inserts a coin.

F1 or Esc (gamepad: Back + Start together): the settings menu (Page Up /
Page Down or LB / RB change its pages): wheels, pedals, buttons, the
picture (presets, size, a CRT look, smoothed pixel art), full screen, the
volume. F3: frame times. F11 or Alt+Enter: full screen. Wheels: a
direct-drive (free-turning) wheel, a mouse or a spinner; see the Controls
page.

Settings and high scores are kept in %LOCALAPPDATA%\qilin\@GAME@ (the Game
page of the menu shows the folder), with the ROM folder you chose and the
build's cache of compiled files (build-cache).


Checking a wheel and performance
--------------------------------
Once the game is built, double-click "Check controls and performance.bat".
It starts a normal session with an input recording, performance timings and
a controller report, in a new folder under "Hardware checks" with a
checklist printed in the window: one wheel setup, pedals and buttons, full
turns, pausing, Alt-Tab and reconnecting, then two minutes of play, then
quit normally. Fill in the checklist; nothing is uploaded. The controller
report includes serials and device paths; the recording includes the
starting high scores and settings, but no ROMs.


What's in here
--------------
Play @TITLE@.exe        chooses your ROMs, builds the game (once), starts it
kit\qilin.exe       the recompiler: turns the ROMs' programs into C++
kit\lib, include    the prebuilt rest of the game: the board, video, sound,
                    the window and controls (SDL3), the menu (Dear ImGui)
kit\toolchain       LLVM-MinGW, a C++ compiler for Windows (Clang)
kit\files.txt       every file this release holds (see below)
work\               made when building: the game (@EXE@), built from your
                    ROMs, the recompiled code, the build's files and the logs
LICENSES\           the licences of everything included

Source, changes and issues: https://github.com/Qilin1066/ApbArcade--QilinRecomp


Updates and recovery
--------------------
"Check for updates" in Play @TITLE@.exe asks GitHub for a newer release
(it sends nothing about you or your PC). If there is one, it downloads it,
unpacks it beside this folder and swaps in the new kit and launcher, then
starts again and builds the game for the new version. If anything fails on
the way, the old version is left as it was. You can also unzip a new
download anywhere, even over this folder: it finds your ROM folder and the
cache by itself, and at its first start it removes what an older version
left behind (the Play @TITLE@.bat and play.ps1 of the earlier downloads, files
the new kit no longer has: anything in kit\ or LICENSES\ that kit\files.txt
doesn't name). Your settings and high scores are never in this folder, so
nothing of yours is touched. (Downloads before the launcher kept the ROM
folder in apb.ini only: choose it once more.)

The game is compiled for this PC's processor; moved to another PC, it is
built again. Compiled files come from the cache when nothing they're made
from has changed. A failed build leaves the working game as it was; the one
before a new build is kept as work\@EXE@.previous until the new one has run
and closed normally. "Build again from scratch" compiles everything anew.
